Cell["\<\
layers is an ordered association layerIndex -> pointList. For two or more \
layers the output is {diagonalBlocks, lowerBlocks}.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1978644723,ExpressionUUID->"f4a2e74a-41c1-ed4d-8ad9-42252fab1f47"],

Cell["\<\
lowerBlocks[[i]] has rows in layer i+1 and columns in layer i. \
Nonadjacent-layer couplings are not included.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1897214615,ExpressionUUID->"b4dadac7-e82d-8d42-bea5-f42af788e9e5"],

Cell["\<\
For a single layer, this implementation returns the Hamiltonian matrix itself \
rather than a two-list block representation.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->912691942,ExpressionUUID->"2c28f63d-0bc2-e347-848e-6c993d8843ff"],

Cell["The underlying hopping cutoff must be a Real.", "Notes",
 CellID->829392354,ExpressionUUID->"90f9f793-eb3e-c742-ad99-d2fc6f230c1e"],

Cell["\<\
Checks every consecutive three-layer window for coupling between its first \
and third layers and prints diagnostics. A failed check prints a request to \
reduce the division number and returns no block result.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1016611256,ExpressionUUID->"506e790b-929c-1b4d-b037-772261cb5fb0"]
}, Closed]],

